    "us-cs-yale": {
      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["ACT or SAT required — all first-year and transfer applicants, from the 2026–27 cycle","Other exams, including international leaving exams and English proficiency exams, do not fulfil this requirement"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/standardized-testing","label":"Yale: Standardized Testing"},{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/posts/2026-08-17-application-update-2026-2027","label":"Yale: Application Update 2026–2027"},{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/international","label":"Yale: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["All first-year and transfer applicants must include scores from the ACT or SAT.","Starting with this cycle, we will be requiring all first-year and transfer applicants to submit either the SAT or the ACT.","Scores from other exams, including international leaving exams or English proficiency exams will not fulfill Yale’s testing requirement."],"reviewFlag":"data/courseRequirements.js still records usAdmissions.test \"flexible\" (test-flexible) for this course; Yale now requires the ACT or SAT. Owner decision — not changed here."},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["English proficiency test required for non-native English speakers without two or more years of enrollment in an English-medium school","Tests listed: TOEFL iBT, IELTS, Cambridge English (C1 Advanced, C2 Proficiency or B2 First), Duolingo English Test; InitialView interviews are also listed"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/standardized-testing","label":"Yale: Standardized Testing"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you are a non-native English speaker without two or more years of enrollment in an English-medium school, you are required to submit scores from an English proficiency test, in addition to fulfilling Yale’s standardized testing requirement with ACT or SAT scores.","note":"Yale publishes the scores of its most competitive applicants, not minimum scores, so no score is shown as a requirement."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/requirements","label":"Yale: First-year requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"First-year applications include letters of recommendation, a transcript, and standardized test scores."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/course-selection","label":"Yale: Course Selection"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Yale does not prescribe a set of secondary school courses that are required for admission. … Generally speaking, you should try to take courses each year in English, science, math, the social sciences, and foreign language.","note":"Official: Yale has no required secondary-school courses, but advises taking courses each year in English, science, math, the social sciences and foreign language. This applies to all Yale College applicants, whatever the intended major.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists advised high-school subjects (English, science, math, social sciences, foreign language), while stating none are required; data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"partial","accepted":"unknown","detail":"International leaving-exam results do not fulfil Yale’s ACT/SAT requirement; applicants from schools outside the U.S. meet the same requirements as all other applicants.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/international","label":"Yale: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Scores from other exams, including international leaving exams or English proficiency exams will not fulfill Yale’s testing requirement. … Students applying from secondary schools outside the U.S. complete the same applications and fulfill the same application requirements as all other applicants.","note":"Yale’s pages do not mention A-Levels by name — this row applies Yale’s statement on international leaving exams."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"unknown","detail":"IB scores, including predicted IB scores, are optional (encouraged for students with IB coursework) and no longer fulfil the ACT/SAT requirement.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/standardized-testing","label":"Yale: Standardized Testing"},{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/posts/2026-08-17-application-update-2026-2027","label":"Yale: Application Update 2026–2027"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Including AP or IB scores is not required but is encouraged for students who have completed AP- or IB-designated coursework. Applicants may submit predicted IB scores, if available, but these are not required.","But we gave them four options– SAT, ACT, AP, or IB. And moving forward, that list of options is just going to be narrowed to just the SAT or the ACT."]},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP scores are optional — encouraged for students with AP coursework, self-reported alongside ACT/SAT scores","AP scores no longer fulfil the ACT/SAT requirement"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/standardized-testing","label":"Yale: Standardized Testing"},{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/posts/2026-08-17-application-update-2026-2027","label":"Yale: Application Update 2026–2027"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["If you have completed AP or IB exams, you may include the scores of your choosing in the testing section of your application along with your ACT or SAT score(s). Including AP or IB scores is not required but is encouraged for students who have completed AP- or IB-designated coursework.","But we gave them four options– SAT, ACT, AP, or IB. And moving forward, that list of options is just going to be narrowed to just the SAT or the ACT."]},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Interviews: by invitation only; not required","Supplementary arts portfolio (music, visual art, film, dance) or STEM research: optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/interviews","label":"Yale: Interviews"},{"url":"https://admissions.yale.edu/supplementary","label":"Yale: Supplementary Materials"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Alumni volunteers and current Yale students conduct evaluative interviews, by invitation only. … Interviews are not required, and many successful applicants are not interviewed.","First-year and transfer applicants may supplement their application with an arts portfolio or academic research."]}
    },
