      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Columbia accepts all secondary school curricula, including the International Baccalaureate, and reviews applications in the context of the curriculum. the International Baccalaureate results must be submitted if they are required to complete and graduate from secondary school; otherwise they are not required.","sources":[{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/international","label":"Columbia: International Applicants"},{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/process/testing","label":"Columbia: Testing Policy"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Columbia accepts all secondary school curricula (e.g., International Baccalaureate, Cambridge A Levels, National School curricula, etc.), and applications are reviewed within the context of your curriculum. Internal and external exam results—such as A Level, International Baccalaureate, French Baccalaureate, Advanced Placement (AP) exams, and other final national exam results—must be submitted if they are required to complete and graduate from secondary school. If they are not required for the completion of and graduation from secondary school, you are not required to submit results.","Please note that any proficiency exam scores that are required for the completion of, and graduation from, your secondary school must be submitted. This may include internal and external exam results, such as A Level, International Baccalaureate, French Baccalaureate, and other final national exam results."],"note":"Columbia states no IB points requirement."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP scores are not required; you may submit them in the testing section and not submitting is no disadvantage","AP results must be submitted if they are required to complete and graduate from your secondary school"],"sources":[{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/process/testing","label":"Columbia: Testing Policy"},{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/international","label":"Columbia: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Advanced Placement (AP) and other optional standardized exam scores are not required by Columbia, but we will accept your results if you choose to submit them in the testing section of your Common App or Coalition Application. We do often find them helpful in our review. You will not be at a disadvantage in our admissions process should you choose not to take these optional tests or submit the scores to Columbia.","Columbia accepts all secondary school curricula (e.g., International Baccalaureate, Cambridge A Levels, National School curricula, etc.), and applications are reviewed within the context of your curriculum. Internal and external exam results—such as A Level, International Baccalaureate, French Baccalaureate, Advanced Placement (AP) exams, and other final national exam results—must be submitted if they are required to complete and graduate from secondary school. If they are not required for the completion of and graduation from secondary school, you are not required to submit results."]},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Columbia-specific application questions required","Two teacher recommendations from academic disciplines required — for Columbia Engineering, one must be from a math or science teacher","Interviews are not part of the application process","Supplementary materials (arts portfolio, research abstract, resume): optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/firstyear","label":"Columbia: First-Year Applicants"},{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/firstyear","label":"Columbia: First-Year Applicants"},{"url":"https://undergrad.admissions.columbia.edu/apply/firstyear","label":"Columbia: First-Year Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["In addition to the Coalition Application and the Common Application, you must also respond to Columbia-specific questions to provide the Committee on Admissions with a fuller sense of you as a person—including your academic, extracurricular and intellectual interests.","Columbia requires two teacher recommendations. These recommendations must come from teachers who taught you in academic disciplines (e.g., English and/or language arts, math, science, social studies and/or social science, or world language). For applicants to Columbia Engineering, one of the teacher recommendations must come from a math or science teacher.","Supplementary materials, such as an arts portfolio, research abstract or resume, are not a required part of our admissions process—but there are occasions where they can enhance our understanding of your application. … Interviews are not a part of the application process."]}
