      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"If you will take the IB on completing school, your school official should include predicted marks with the secondary school report. IB results do not replace the required SAT/ACT.","sources":[{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/305-what-educational-records-are-required-for-international-students/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: Educational records for international students"},{"url":"https://admissions.cornell.edu/policies/standardized-testing-policy","label":"Cornell: Standardized Testing Policy"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["If there is a provincial, national, or other board exam an applicant will take on completing school (A-Levels, Higher Secondary Certificate, IB., German Abitur, etc.), the school official providing the secondary school report should include the predicted marks.","First-year applicants are required to submit SAT or ACT scores when applying to Cornell."]},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP scores are not required; you may submit them if you wish"],"sources":[{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/412-does-cornell-university-require-advanced-placement-ap-exam-scores/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: Does Cornell require AP exam scores?"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Applicants to Cornell University are not required to submit Advanced Placement (AP) exam scores. Students who have taken AP exams and wish to submit their scores are welcome to do so."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Apply directly to one Cornell college or school; applications are reviewed by that college","Cornell supplement with college-specific essay(s) required; two teacher recommendations required","Personal interviews not required or available (except Architecture)","Arts & Sciences: one 650-word college essay"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.cornell.edu/how-to-apply/first-year-applicants","label":"Cornell: First-Year Applicants"},{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/296-as-an-international-student-how-will-my-application-be-read/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: How will my application be read?"},{"url":"https://admissions.cornell.edu/how-to-apply/first-year-applicants","label":"Cornell: First-Year Applicants"},{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/179-does-cornell-require-personal-interviews/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: Does Cornell require personal interviews?"},{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/479-what-are-the-essay-questions-for-the-fall-2027-application/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: Essay questions for the Fall 2027 application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["At Cornell, you'll apply directly to one of our colleges or schools; be sure to explore your options to choose your best fit. Once you've made your decision, review unique application requirements for that college or school by clicking the appropriate link below.","All applications are reviewed by the specific Cornell college or school to which a student has applied.","Submit your Common Application online. … You're required to submit two teacher recommendations, which should highlight your academic strengths and contributions in the classroom. … As part of your Common Application, you'll be asked to fill out the Cornell University supplement, which includes the college- or school-specific essay(s) you'll need to answer. … You're required to submit SAT or ACT scores when applying to Cornell.","Personal interviews are not required, nor available, for admission to any of Cornell's other undergraduate level programs.","In the online Common Application Writing Supplement for those applying for Fall 2027 entry, students will complete only the essay(s) that correspond to the undergraduate college or school to which you are applying."]}
